# Database dumps.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not cosmetic. A pattern like
# `supabase/` with no slash matches a directory of that name at ANY depth — so
# it also swallowed `lib/work/supabase/`, the four Supabase client modules the
# entire workspace imports. They were never committed, the local build kept
# passing because the files were on disk, and the first fresh clone (Vercel)
# failed with 21 "Can't resolve '@/lib/work/supabase/server'" errors.
#
# The whole tree is local-only, one folder per Supabase project:
#   supabase/site/   portfolio + newtab + admin (one project)
#   supabase/shop/   shop
#   supabase/work/   work — schema.sql/storage.sql are generated by
#                    `npm run work:db:snapshot` from supabase/work/migrations/
# Nothing here is committed: a fresh database is rebuilt from the work
# migrations and otherwise filled through the admin UI.
#
# Anchor every directory rule meant for the repo root.
/supabase/

# Unanchored, so it also hides `app/newtab/` — the route the ecosystem page
# links to. Left as-is rather than changed here: this fix is for the build
# break, and un-ignoring it adds files that were never meant to be in the
# commit that repairs the deploy.
newtab/
!components/newtab/
!components/newtab/**

# Generated SQL bundles from scripts/bundle-work-migrations.mjs. The migrations
# in supabase/work/migrations/ are the source of truth; these are throwaway
# copies made for pasting into a SQL editor.
/apply-*.sql
/verify-*.sql
